"These intrinsics previously only set masked-off lanes to poison, and will be "
"automatically upgraded to their non-VP equivalent.  On RISC-V the VL "
"optimizer should automatically infer `vl` in most cases from a store or "
"reduction instruction, so passing around an explicit EVL operand shouldn't "
"be required. If needed a \"root\" EVL can be synthesized with "
"`llvm.vp.merge`, e.g:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:161
msgid ""
"The `llvm.vp.merge` will be folded away but the `%evl` will be propagated to "
"the add instruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:164
msgid ""
"The `llvm.strip.invariant.group` intrinsic has been removed. It existed to "
"work around a bug relating to replacement of pointers with different "
"provenance based on dominating equality conditions, and is no longer needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:168
msgid ""
"Introduced the generic `!atomic.ignore.denormal.mode` metadata for floating-"
"point `atomicrmw` instructions, generalizing the previously AMDGPU-specific "
"`!amdgpu.ignore.denormal.mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:172
msgid ""
"Added the `bitinsert` and `bitextract` instructions for bit-range "
"manipulation on byte type values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:175
msgid "Changes to LLVM infrastructure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:177
msgid ""
"Removed `TargetOptions::FloatABIType`. The soft float ABI should be "
"controlled by setting the `\"float-abi\"` module flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:180
msgid ""
"Removed `TargetOptions::ExceptionModel`. The exception model should be "
"controlled by setting the `\"exception-model\"` module flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:183
msgid ""
"Removed `TargetOptions::EABIVersion` and the `llc`/`opt` `-meabi` flag. The "
"GNU-vs-EABI distinction is now derived entirely from the target triple's "
"environment (e.g. `arm-none-gnueabi` vs `arm-none-eabi`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:187
msgid ""
"Replaced `TargetOptions::EnableMachineFunctionSplitter` with "
"`TargetOptions::FunctionSplitting`, and the `-split-machine-functions` and `-"
"enable-split-machine-functions` flags with `-function-"
"splitting={none,bbsections,all}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:191
msgid ""
"Backend tools (`llc`, `opt`, LTO plugin options and libLTO debug options): "
"use `-function-splitting=all` for the previous behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:193
msgid ""
"Clang and Flang: `-fsplit-machine-functions` is unchanged and remains the "
"recommended spelling. `-mllvm -enable-split-machine-functions` should be "
"replaced with `-fsplit-machine-functions` or `-mllvm -function-"
"splitting=all`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:198
msgid ""
"Merged the `MachineFunctionSplitter` pass into the `BasicBlockSections` "
"pass, which now performs all function splitting: it uses the basic block "
"sections profile where available, and the PGO/AutoFDO profile elsewhere "
"(with `-function-splitting=all`). `createMachineFunctionSplitterPass()` and "
"the `machine-function-splitter` pass name are removed; "
"`createBasicBlockSectionsPass()` takes a `SplitWithPGO` argument instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:205
msgid ""
"Removed the legacy pass manager's `RegionPass` and `RGPassManager` classes, "
"which no longer had any users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:208
msgid "Changes to building LLVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:210
msgid ""
"A new `LLVM_ENABLE_LZMA` option (`ON`, `OFF` or `FORCE_ON`; default `ON`) "
"controls whether LLVM links liblzma for xz decompression. It replaces LLDB's "
"`LLDB_ENABLE_LZMA`, which is deprecated: a monorepo build maps it onto "
"`LLVM_ENABLE_LZMA`, and it has no effect in a standalone LLDB build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:215
msgid ""
"The DirectX backend is now an official target and has moved from "
"`LLVM_ALL_EXPERIMENTAL_TARGETS` to `LLVM_ALL_TARGETS`. It is now built by "
"default and no longer requires `LLVM_EXPERIMENTAL_TARGETS_TO_BUILD`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:219
msgid ""
"Clang and MLIR projects enabled implicitly as Flang dependencies now omit "
"unrelated build and test targets. Installation retains the dependency "
"libraries, headers, resources, and CMake targets needed by Flang. Explicitly "
"enabling Clang or MLIR retains the project's complete build, test, and "
"install behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:225
msgid ""
"With `CLANG_ENABLE_CIR=ON` and `mlir` in `LLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS`, "
"`find_package(Clang)` now looks for the associated MLIR CMake package before "
"importing Clang's targets, so consumers no longer need to call "
"`find_package(MLIR)` themselves and can do so in either order. As a "
"consequence the consumer's project also sees the `MLIR_*` variables and "
"targets, as it already does for Flang. When MLIR is only an implicit ClangIR "
"dependency, its build-tree `MLIRConfig.cmake` now reports the package as not "
"found with an explanatory message instead of succeeding with no targets; "
"such a build never provided a usable MLIR SDK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:235
msgid ""
"When Clang is in the `LLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS` list, it now compiles the "
"experimental MLIR-Generator ClangIR by default. This functionality can "
"increase the compile time and binary size of Clang significantly.  This can "
"be disabled with `CLANG_ENABLE_CIR=OFF`, which wil disable the `-fclangir` "
"flag in Clang."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:241
msgid ""
"LLVM's documentation has largely been rewritten from [reStructuredText] to "
"Markdown, and our Sphinx documentation build now has a hard dependency on "
"the [`myst-parser` package]. Vendors packaging LLVM will need to install "
"`myst-parser` to generate HTML or man page documentation. For convenience, "
"we now release a `llvm_man_pages-${VER}.tar.xz` tarball if you need man page "
"docs on a minimal system without Sphinx or `myst-parser`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:251
msgid "Changes to the Windows installer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:253
msgid ""
"The project has migrated to MSI installers. Previous installations of LLVM, "
"prior (and including) 23.1.0, must be manually uninstalled first, before "
"installing this new release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:257
msgid "Changes to TableGen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:259
msgid ""
"`!cond` operator short-circuits at the first `true` condition.  Subsequent "
"`condition : value` pairs, along with their corresponding side effects, are "
"left unresolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:263
msgid "Changes to Interprocedural Optimizations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:265
msgid ""
"Interprocedural passes no longer rewrite the signature of functions marked "
"`optnone`, so their argument list, return type, and calling convention are "
"preserved. Interprocedural analysis and transformation of such functions is "
"otherwise unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:270
msgid ""
"The IR Outliner has been removed, due to lack of a maintainer and the "
"presence of correctness issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:273
msgid "Changes to Vectorizers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:275
msgid "Changes to the AArch64 Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:277
msgid "Added support for C2-Pro and C2-Ultra CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:278
msgid ""
"Added support for hardening return address signing against PACMAN attacks. "
"Functions with the `\"sign-return-address-harden\"=\"load-return-address\"` "
"attribute perform a load from the return address before returning, reducing "
"the cache side channel used to guess pointer authentication codes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:283
msgid ""
"The SelectionDAG Darwin ABI lowering of function arguments which are "
"aggregates passed by value containing small integers less than 32 bits in "
"size has been made consistent with the GlobalISel lowering of such "
"arguments. This is an ABI-breaking change but is unlikely to have any "
"observable effect from higher-level languages compiled through clang."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:289
msgid ""
"Assembler/disassembler support has been added for Armv9.8-A (2026) "
"architecture extensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:292
msgid ""
"Added support for the `aarch64-unknown-uefi` target. It follows the Windows "
"ARM64 ABI (calling convention, callee saved registers, stack probing and SEH "
"unwind information) and produces PE/COFF objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:296
msgid "Changes to the AMDGPU Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:298
msgid ""
"Replaced `xnack` and `sramecc` target features with `amdgpu.xnack` and "
"`amdgpu.sramecc` module flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:300
msgid ""
"`llvm.amdgcn.make.buffer.rsrc` now accepts any integer width for its "
"`numRecords` argument to account for targets that use 32-bit and 45-bit "
"`numRecords` widths more accurately. If an integer of the incorrect width is "
"used, it will be zero-extended or truncated as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:305
msgid "These intrinsics have been removed in favour of `llvm.amdgcn.ballot`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:306
msgid "`llvm.amdgcn.icmp`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:307
msgid "`llvm.amdgcn.fcmp`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:309
msgid "Changes to the ARM Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:311
msgid ""
"Using the hard-float procedure call standard without floating-point "
"registers is now an error. Previously this would fall back to the soft-float "
"PCS while still emitting the hard-float ABI attribute tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:315
msgid "Changes to the AVR Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:317
msgid "Changes to the BPF Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:319
msgid ""
"Added `-mcpu=v5`, which includes the v4 instruction set and enables unsigned "
"and signed high-half multiply instructions (`UHMUL` and `SHMUL`). Use `-"
"disable-hmul` to disable their generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:323
msgid "Changes to the DirectX Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:325
msgid ""
"The DirectX backend has been promoted from experimental to an official, "
"fully supported LLVM target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:328
msgid "Changes to the Hexagon Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:330
msgid "Changes to the LoongArch Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:332
msgid "Changes to the MIPS Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:334
msgid "Changes to the PowerPC Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:336
msgid "Changes to the RISC-V Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:338
msgid ""
"Added experimental MC support for the ACLIC v0.20 extensions: `Smidctrl`, "
"`Ssidctrl`, `Smnip`, `Ssnip`, `Smijt`, `Ssijt`, `Smehv`, `Ssehv`, `Smcsps`, "
"`Sscsps`, `Smip`, and `Ssip`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:341
msgid ""
"Adds experimental assembler/CodeGen support for the `Zilx` (Indexed Integer "
"Load) extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:343
msgid "Bump Svukte extension to 1.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:344
msgid "Remove experimental from Zicfiss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:345
msgid "Added support for `Sspmp`, `Sspmpen` and `Smpmpdeleg` extensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:346
msgid "Removed veyron-v1 processor definition and tuning model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:347
msgid "Removed support for the `Ventana Conditional Operations` extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:348
msgid ""
"Added support for `tail symbol, rt` form that takes an address "
"(materialisation) register, that is used when software guarded branch is "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:350
msgid ""
"Updated the experimental `Zvzip` extension to the v0.3 draft specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:351
msgid "Added the `RVA23P1S64` and `RVB23P1S64` profiles (version 1.0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:352
msgid ""
"Updated the canonical order of one-letter RISC-V extensions to match the "
"latest specification, placing ``p`` after ``v`` and removing unused ``n``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:354
msgid ""
"Adds experimental assembler support for the `Xqccmi` (Qualcomm 16-bit "
"Instruction Lookup Table) vendor extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:355
msgid "Added `-mcpu=gaisler-gr765` for the 64-bit GR765 processor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:356
msgid ""
"Added `-mcpu=tt-ascalon-xg` for the Tenstorrent Ascalon XG processor, the "
"global variant of Ascalon X without `Zvkng` and with reduced vector FP64 "
"throughput."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:360
msgid "Changes to the WebAssembly Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:362
msgid ""
"Added support for emitting common symbols (.comm) using the "
"WASM_SYMBOL_BINDING_COMMON flag (see https://github.com/WebAssembly/tool-"
"conventions/pull/267)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:364
msgid ""
"Added `@llvm.wasm.memory.copy` and `@llvm.wasm.memory.fill` intrinsics for "
"the WebAssembly `memory.copy` and `memory.fill` instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:367
msgid "Changes to the Windows Target"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:369
msgid "Changes to the X86 Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:371
msgid ""
"Added assembler and code generation support for the `AVX10_V2_AUX` "
"instruction set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:373
msgid ""
"The AMX intrinsics that name tile registers (`llvm.x86.tileloadd64`, "
"`llvm.x86.tdpbssd` and the others outside the `_internal` forms) now declare "
"their memory effects: they read or write the tile state as `target_mem0`, "
"and the memory operations access only memory through their pointer argument. "
"Before, each one could read and write any memory, so loads of loop-invariant "
"values weren't hoisted out of loops of tile operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:380
msgid "Changes to the OCaml bindings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:382
msgid ""
"Removed the `size_of` and `align_of` functions. Create a constant based on "
"the result of `DataLayout.abi_size` or `DataLayout.abi_align` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:385
msgid "`DataLayout` has been moved from `Llvm_target` to `Llvm`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:387
msgid ""
"`data_layout` now returns a `DataLayout` instead of a `string`. Similarly "
"`set_data_layout` now accepts a `DataLayout` instead of a `string`. You can "
"use `DataLayout.of_string` and `DataLayout.as_string` to convert between "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:391
msgid ""
"`const_gep` and `const_in_bounds_gep` have been removed in favor of "
"`const_ptradd` and `const_ptradd_from_indices`. Both create `getelementptr "
"i8` constant expressions, the former using an integer offset, and the latter "
"using a data layout, base type and index sequence. The latter API returns an "
"option, as it may fail if the indices cannot be converted into ptradd "
"representation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:397
msgid ""
"The `llcontext` argument of `builder_at`, `builder_before` and "
"`builder_at_end` has been removed. These functions now take only an "
"insertion point, instruction, or block, respectively. The context is implied "
"by the insertion point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:402
msgid "`builder` now takes an `llmodule` argument, instead of `llcontext`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:404
msgid "Changes to the Python bindings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:406
msgid "Changes to the C API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:408
msgid ""
"`LLVMAlignOf()` and `LLVMSizeOf()` have been deprecated. Create a constant "
"based on the result of `LLVMABIAlignmentOfType()` or `LLVMABISizeOfType()` "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:412
msgid ""
"Bindings operating on data layout (`LLVMTargetDataRef`) have been moved from "
"`Target.h` (`Target` library) to `Core.h` (`IR` library)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:415
msgid ""
"`LLVMConstGEP2()`, `LLVMConstInBoundsGEP2()` and "
"`LLVMConstGEPWithNoWrapFlags()` have been deprecated. `LLVMConstPtrAdd()` "
"and `LLVMConstPtrAddFromIndices()` can be used instead. Both create "
"`getelementptr i8` constant expressions, the former using an integer offset, "
"and the latter using a data layout, base type and index sequence. The latter "
"API may fail if the indices cannot be converted into ptradd representation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:423
msgid ""
"Added `LLVMIsDSOLocal()` and `LLVMSetDSOLocal()` to query and set the "
"`dso_local` runtime preemption specifier on global values (global variables, "
"functions and aliases)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:427
msgid ""
"Deprecated `LLVMCreateBuilderInContext()` in favor of "
"`LLVMCreateBuilderForModule()`, which takes a `LLVMModuleRef` instead of "
"`LLVMContextRef`. When using the old API, an insertion point (connected to a "
"module) must be set using a `LLVMPositionBuilder*()` API before building any "
"instructions, otherwise an error will be generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:433
msgid "Changes to the CodeGen infrastructure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:435
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash ([#214750](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/"
"214750)) when compiling a function containing a static alloca of "
"`(size_t)-1` bytes, whose size collided with the sentinel value "
"MachineFrameInfo used to mark dead stack objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:440
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash ([#204079](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/"
"204079)) in the SelectionDAG pre-RA schedulers when they tried to unfold a "
"load-folded instruction to break a physical register dependency and the "
"unfolded load already existed in the DAG."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:445
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash ([#220959](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/"
"220959)) when compiling a `landingpad` whose result type is not a struct of "
"an exception pointer and an integer selector (for example `{}`). Such a "
"landingpad is now rejected with a clean \"unsupported\" diagnostic instead "
"of an assertion failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:452
msgid "Changes to the Metadata Info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:454
msgid "Changes to the Debug Info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:456
msgid "Changes to the LLVM tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:458
msgid ""
"`opt` and `llc` accept `-plugin-arg=<plugin>,<arg>`, which passes `<arg>` to "
"the new `PassPluginLibraryInfo::ParseArguments` callback of the pass plugin "
"named `<plugin>`. A plugin that defines `cl::opt` has to call "
"`cl::ParseCommandLineOptions` itself inside `ParseArguments`. "
"`LLVM_PLUGIN_API_VERSION` is now 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:462
msgid ""
"`opt` and `llc` load `-load-pass-plugin` plugins after parsing the command "
"line, so a loaded plugin's options are no longer accepted as ordinary "
"options. Pass them with `-plugin-arg=<plugin>,<arg>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:465
msgid ""
"llvm-offload-binary can now compress packaged binaries using zstd or zlib."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:467
msgid "llvm-mca no longer defaults -mcpu to \"native\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:469
msgid ""
"llvm-rc now supports `/showIncludes` to report header and resource-file "
"dependencies in a format compatible with Ninja's `deps = msvc` mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:472
msgid "Changes to LLDB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:474
msgid ""
"`platform.plugin.wasm.runtime-args` now precede the port argument on the "
"Wasm runtime's command line instead of following it. A runtime that "
"dispatches on a leading subcommand can therefore name that subcommand "
"through this setting, rather than needing a wrapper script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:478
msgid ""
"MiniDebugInfo (the ELF `.gnu_debugdata` section) is now decompressed by LLVM "
"rather than by LLDB's own liblzma binding, and is enabled with "
"`LLVM_ENABLE_LZMA` instead of the deprecated `LLDB_ENABLE_LZMA`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:482
msgid "SBAPI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:484
msgid ""
"A [bug](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/211787) involving "
"SBValues representing a register set was fixed. The methods "
"`GetIndexOfChildWithName` and `GetChildMemberWithName` were incorrectly "
"looking up values in all register sets. This meant that "
"`GetIndexOfChildWithName` could return an index greater than the size of the "
"set, and that `GetChildMemberWithName` could return values that were "
"actually in a different set. Both methods are now fixed so that they are "
"limited to the registers within the register set. Scripts using these "
"methods may have to be updated as a result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:493
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:495
msgid "Python 3.11 or later is now required for building LLDB 24 on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:496
msgid ""
"For better performance, LLDB now turns off the Windows debug heap by default "
"when debugging. If you need the debug heap enabled, set "
"`platform.plugin.windows.disable-debug-heap` to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:499
msgid "Changes to BOLT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:501
msgid "Changes to Sanitizers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:503
msgid ""
"AddressSanitizer's `operator new` now calls the current `std::new_handler` "
"on allocation failure, as the C++ standard requires. With "
"`allocator_may_return_null=1`, throwing `operator new` throws "
"`std::bad_alloc` instead of aborting (on runtimes built with exceptions), "
"and nothrow `operator new` returns `nullptr`. By default it still aborts "
"once the handler chain is exhausted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:510
msgid "Other Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:512
msgid ""
"`cas::ObjectStore::getMemoryBuffer()` was documented as returning a buffer "
"whose lifetime is independent of the CAS, but the buffer it returns may "
"alias storage the CAS owns and so cannot outlive it. The documentation now "
"matches the behavior, and the new `getStandaloneMemoryBuffer()` provides a "
"buffer that does stay valid after the `ObjectStore` is destroyed."
msgstr ""

